WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.640
It would be difficult to check out everything
leaving Netflix in August, so we have a list

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.840
of the best of the best films you have to
watch before they disappear.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.280
Between now and the end of August, sign into
your Netflix account and load up these movies

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.520
you won’t want to miss.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.340
Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas, Terry Gilliam's
psychedelic satirical black comedy based on

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:22.439
Hunter S. Thompson's book of the same name,
is a flick you either love with every fiber

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.900
of your being, don't really understand, or
haven't seen at all.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.420
Or maybe you just don't like it, because that's
fair too.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.699
The film divided critics upon its release
in May 1998, largely for its pendulous nature

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.860
and bizarreness that can make your head spin.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.380
But in the two decades since, Fear and Loathing
has picked up a swarm of fans who will go

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.160
to bat for it.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.840
Set in 1971, Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas
centers on journalist Raoul Duke and his lawyer,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.180
Dr. Gonzo, as they take a road trip from the
sunny skies of Los Angeles to the sin-filled

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.560
deserts of Las Vegas.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.570
What begins as an effort to document a race
devolves into an exploration of an otherworldly

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.260
dystopia that gets more and more haunting
the further Duke and Gonzo venture in.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.440
"There was evidence in this room of excessive
consumption of almost every type of drug known

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.440
to civilized man since 1544 AD."

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.820
Some think Fear and Loathing is Gilliam's
worst film by a mile, while others have called

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.660
it, quote, "a stylish and faithful adaptation
of a lasting classic of American literature."

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.290
Hurry and find out which side of the argument
you fall on, or revisit an old favorite, before

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.660
Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas departs from
Netflix on August 1st.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.260
Want to indulge in some silly scares as summer
winds down?

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.560
Before August 1st, load up Netflix and watch
the first four installments in the over-the-top

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.580
horror franchise Final Destination.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.390
Each entry in the saga centers on a group
of young adults who fight for their lives

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.340
after a friend of theirs is suddenly struck
with a vision and warns they will all die

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.720
in a freak accident.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.340
All seems okay when the group isn't involved
in the accident their friend foretold, but

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:53.990
the hand of fate soon swoops down and plucks
them off one by one, killing them via elaborate

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.240
Rube Goldberg-style coincidences.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.140
There's no avoiding Death or their final destination:
the grave.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.180
Though none of the Final Destination movies
have been critical hits, they've performed

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.060
fairly well at the box office and have amassed
something of a cult following.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.020
They're campy and inane, and the perfect movies
to mindlessly watch after a long summer day

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.460
spent lounging in the sun.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.400
Writer-director Edgar Wright and writer-actor
Simon Pegg started the Three Flavours Cornetto

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:25.860
trilogy with 2004's zombie romp Shaun of the
Dead, then built it out with 2007's Hot Fuzz.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:31.120
The comedy stars Pegg as London police constable
Nicholas Angel and his Shaun of the Dead co-star,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.300
Nick Frost, as Angel's overeager partner,
Danny Butterman.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.280
"There was a bit earlier on that you missed
when I distracted him in the Cuddly Monkey

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.260
and then I said 'Playtime's over' and I hit
him with the peace lily."

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.240
"You're off the f---ing chain!"

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.540
After Angel realizes that his flawless track
record of catching baddies has made his London

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.980
superiors angry, he's transferred to the quiet
town of Sandford and partnered up with the

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.840
action movie aficionado Butterman.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.150
Angel reluctantly settles into the calmness
of the countryside town and gets used to having

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.970
the oafish Butterman at his side, but things
take a dark turn when a string of "accidents"

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.420
unleashes horror and chaos onto Sandford.

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:10.300
The two cops buddy up to discover the culprit
and true meaning behind the crimes.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.810
Hot Fuzz, regarded as "everything an action-comedy
should be," leaves Netflix on August 1st,

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.080
in case you didn't already know.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.760
"Nobody tells me nothin."

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:26.440
Directed and co-written by Luc Besson, The
Fifth Element takes place in the 23rd century,

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.239
when Earth is on the brink of collapse hundreds
of years after a race of aliens collected

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.460
four elemental stones from Egypt in 1914.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.500
It's up to Korben Dallas, an ex-special forces
major and current flying taxicab driver, and

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:43.760
Leeloo, an orange-haired humanoid who crashes
into said taxicab, to combine the four elemental

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.790
stones with the fifth element to prevent a
massive ball of flaming death from hurtling

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.740
into the planet.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:52.500
Dallas and Leeloo meet a host of colorful
characters along the way, which makes their

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.540
already unforgettable experience that much
more memorable.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:59.440
Be sure to catch The Fifth Element before
it leaves Netflix on August 1st.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.980
Got your Twinkies?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.180
Got your shotgun?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:06.000
Well, get ready to roll, 'cause the zombie
apocalypse is about to be over, and you don't

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.580
want to miss your shot at killing some undead
creatures.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.900
Ruben Fleischer's runaway hit horror-comedy
Zombieland follows a group of four humans

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.420
roaming the zombie apocalypse.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.820
Making his way from his dorm room in Texas
to Ohio to see if his parents are still alive,

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.830
geeky college kid Columbus meets three strangers
who become his makeshift family: sisters Wichita

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.170
and Little Rock, who have some unique ways
of dealing with chaos, and zombie-killing

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.360
expert Tallahassee.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.240
There's humor and gore, violence and a kickin'
soundtrack, an appearance from Bill Murray

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.460
as a fictionalized version of himself, and
even some romance - you know, something for

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:37.960
everyone.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.500
Zombieland is set to jump off Netflix on the
very first day of August, so hop to it.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.860
Then, look forward to catching the sequel,
Zombieland: Double Tap, in theaters on October

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:47.360
18th.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:52.360
Javier Bardem has taken his fair share of
turns as baddies in films like Skyfall and

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:56.530
Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No
Tales, but no villainous character Bardem

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:01.360
has embodied comes close to the psychopathic
assassin Anton Chigurh in No Country for Old

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:01.860
Men.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:08.420
"What business is it of yours where I'm from,
friendo?"

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:15.480
Set up as a cat-and-mouse game, No Country
for Old Men begins with a discovery: Llewelyn

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:20.850
Moss steps into the aftermath of a drug deal
gone wrong, and finds $2 million in cash sitting

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.800
in the back of a truck.

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:26.020
It's an unexpected payday for Moss, but it
changes his life forever when Chigurh sets

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.140
out to recover the money.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:32.420
An adaptation of Cormac McCarthy's novel of
the same name, No Country for Old Men is thrilling

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:36.940
and bleakly funny as it explores themes of
religion and fate against the arid backdrop

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.160
of the Lone Star State.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.960
Your last chance to catch it on Netflix is
August 11th.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:46.080
Directed by Garth Jennings in his feature
debut, The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.060
brings the weird and wonderful novels of the
late Douglas Adams to life in a way that no

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.260
previous adaptations could really manage.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:52.980
"Excuse me"

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.420
The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy centers
on Arthur Dent, an English everyman who's

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.500
having a particularly troubling day.

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:08.160
He learns that his house is scheduled for
a bulldozing, that his friend, Ford Prefect,

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:12.340
is actually an alien journalist, and that
Earth will be demolished to clear space in

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.760
the solar system for a hyperspace bypass.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:19.560
Arthur's only shot at surviving is to hitch
a ride on a passing spacecraft, and thus he

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.840
embarks on a journey he never could've imagined.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.300
Our unlikely hero discovers that everything
he thought he knew about life has been wrong,

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.730
and everything he needs to know rests in a
book called The Hitchhiker's Guide to the

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:30.380
Galaxy.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.930
Also starring Zooey Deschanel as a humanoid
named Trillian, Hitchhiker's Guide has been

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.120
hailed as a delightful sci-fi treat, and it
leaves Netflix on August 20th.

